    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): [ev-f752f3803a17] says the `crossplane render` command now uses an explicitly set XR `Ready` state value (a feature from PR 6021) that it previously ignored. [ev-56218e966004] shows the change is limited to the render CLI code (cmd/crank/render/render.go and its test). That is enough to write the open aspects: exposure is people running `crossplane render` on XRs whose composition sets an explicit Ready state, and the consequence is that render output now shows that Ready state instead of ignoring it. Nothing in the changed files suggests a cluster runtime effect. Confidence is low because PR 6021, which defines the explicit Ready mechanism and what render shows, is not in the evidence.",
